M4 AUDIO / VOICE / TRANSITION SMOKE — Technical, non-canon test. Use normal click/Space advance after every visible checkpoint. #line:0ee619d

<<vn_bg m3_bg_a>>
<<vn_clear_cg>>
CHECKPOINT SETUP-01 — Background A must be visible. No CG or character should be required for this first audio section. #line:0f9eeb1

<<bgm_play m4_bgm_a>>
CHECKPOINT BGM-01 — BGM A must be audible now. #line:048595e

CHECKPOINT BGM-02 — BGM A must be configured to loop. Let it continue long enough to confirm it remains playing; it must not stop at its clip end. #line:064993a

ANNOUNCEMENT BGM-03 — Next, BGM A crossfades to BGM B over two seconds. Listen for the overlap. #line:02eabdd

<<bgm_crossfade m4_bgm_b 2>>
CHECKPOINT BGM-04 — BGM B alone must now be audible; BGM A must no longer be audible. #line:071d523

ANNOUNCEMENT BGM-05 — Identify BGM B's current musical position. On advance it will fade to silence and pause, preserving that position. #line:0820338

<<bgm_pause 1>>
CHECKPOINT BGM-06 — BGM must be silent while paused. On advance it will resume from the identified position, not restart from the beginning. #line:0eca5fa

<<bgm_resume 1>>
CHECKPOINT BGM-07 — BGM B must resume from its paused position rather than from the start. #line:027b231

ANNOUNCEMENT BGM-08 — On advance, BGM B will fade-stop over one second. #line:0585957

<<bgm_stop 1>>
CHECKPOINT BGM-09 — BGM must now be silent. #line:030e8d0

ANNOUNCEMENT SFX-01 — On advance, one UI-confirm SFX will play. #line:02d8ec6

<<sfx_play ui_confirm>>
CHECKPOINT SFX-02 — One UI-confirm SFX must have played. #line:017c9c1

ANNOUNCEMENT SFX-03 — On advance, UI-confirm will be requested twice immediately. Hear two overlapping/repeated one-shots; the first must not be forcibly cancelled. #line:05b52cb

<<sfx_play ui_confirm>>
<<sfx_play ui_confirm>>
CHECKPOINT SFX-04 — The quick double UI-confirm request must have produced two audible plays or a clearly overlapping double sound. #line:08f8e6d

ANNOUNCEMENT SFX-05 — On advance, the door-close SFX will play. #line:0193e6c

<<sfx_play door_close>>
CHECKPOINT SFX-06 — The door-close SFX must have played. #line:0d78278

CHECKPOINT VOICE-01 — The next named line uses the explicit M4 voice line ID. Listen for its voice clip. #line:0f0acb7

M3 A: VOICE TEST — This line must play the M4 test voice clip. When the clip finishes, this line must remain until you manually advance it. #line:m4_voice_test

CHECKPOINT VOICE-02 — This following non-voice line must not play any stale voice audio. #line:01b3c39

ANNOUNCEMENT SCREEN-01 — On advance, the screen will fade fully to black. The next checkpoint is intentionally behind the black overlay; after confirming black, press Advance to restore the screen. #line:0ff63a6

<<vn_fade_to_black 1>>
CHECKPOINT SCREEN-02 — The screen must now be fully black. After a manual verification pause, advance to fade back in. #line:0f07805

<<vn_fade_from_black 1>>
CHECKPOINT SCREEN-03 — The screen must be restored, with Background A still visible. #line:0b96a94

<<vn_bg m3_bg_a>>
