ANNOUNCEMENT BG-02 — On advance, Background A will crossfade to Background B over two seconds. #line:0775e3c

<<vn_bg_crossfade m3_bg_b 2>>
CHECKPOINT BG-03 — Background B alone must be visible after the crossfade; no stale Background A layer should remain. #line:0923a9c

<<vn_show m3_a default left>>
CHECKPOINT CHAR-01 — Character A must appear normally at Left with Body and default Head visible. #line:042dbda

ANNOUNCEMENT CHAR-02 — On advance, Character A will fade out. Watch the entire layered character, including Body and Head. #line:0d36734

<<vn_hide_fade m3_a 1>>
CHECKPOINT CHAR-03 — Character A must now be hidden. #line:061855c

ANNOUNCEMENT CHAR-04 — On advance, Character A will fade back in. Body and Head must fade together. #line:0047bb8

<<vn_show_fade m3_a default left 1>>
CHECKPOINT CHAR-05 — Character A must be fully visible at Left. Body and Head must have faded together without Image RGB tint being overwritten. #line:033f11a

<<vn_show m3_b default right>>
CHECKPOINT CHAR-06 — Character B must appear immediately at Right; this prepares the speaker-focus regression check. #line:0e8576a

M3 A: CHECKPOINT CHAR-07 — A must be active RGB brightness and B dimmed by M3 speaker focus, while both characters remain fully opaque after their CanvasGroup fades. #line:085b0ac

M3 B: CHECKPOINT CHAR-08 — B must be active RGB brightness and A dimmed. This confirms M3 speaker tint remains compatible with M4 alpha. #line:03f1f83

